["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A covey keeps a tight daily routine: roost, call, feed, grit, dust, rest, feed, call, roost. Be where they will be, at the hour they will be there.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Twenty four hour clock of a quail day in fall, general pattern from bird guides and Washington Fish and Wildlife, 70 to 75 percent. Night: roost in dense trees or shrubs. First light: the covey leaves the roost after assembly calls. Morning: feed and pick grit at road edges. Midday: loaf in cover, dust bathe and drink. Late afternoon: feed again. Dusk: a calling chorus, then roost.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A quail day (October, general pattern)</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 66.0 A92 92 0 0 1 291.2 170.0 L251.6 164.8 A52 52 0 0 0 200.0 106.0 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M291.2 170.0 A92 92 0 0 1 285.0 193.2 L248.0 177.9 A52 52 0 0 0 251.6 164.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M285.0 193.2 A92 92 0 0 1 235.2 243.0 L219.9 206.0 A52 52 0 0 0 248.0 177.9 Z\" fill=\"#e89b5c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M235.2 243.0 A92 92 0 0 1 134.9 223.1 L163.2 194.8 A52 52 0 0 0 219.9 206.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M134.9 223.1 A92 92 0 0 1 108.8 170.0 L148.4 164.8 A52 52 0 0 0 163.2 194.8 Z\" fill=\"#e89b5c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M108.8 170.0 A92 92 0 0 1 108.8 146.0 L148.4 151.2 A52 52 0 0 0 148.4 164.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M108.8 146.0 A92 92 0 0 1 200.0 66.0 L200.0 106.0 A52 52 0 0 0 148.4 151.2 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"131.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n<text x=\"232.0\" y=\"163.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"195.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text x=\"168.0\" y=\"163.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">first light:</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">leave roost</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">feed + grit</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">loaf, dust, water</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">feed again</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dusk calls</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">roost in trees</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A sketch from bird guides (70 to 75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Two feeds: just after dawn and late afternoon <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Midday: loaf in cover, dust bathe, drink <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the day in full</summary><ul><li>\"During the non breeding season, quail feed twice a day, in the morning just after dawn and again in late afternoon.\" (70%, Edgewood notes from Calkins et al.)</li><li>Birds leave the night roost, generally off the ground in trees, between first light and sunrise; assembly calls start the move <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>They pick grit at road and trail edges before the morning and afternoon feeds (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>Midday: rest in moderate to heavy cover, dust bathe, or take water in warm, dry weather <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Dusk: a chorus of calls as they gather to roost <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Legal hunting hours: 1 hour before sunrise to 1 hour after sunset (99%, Rule Book).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>From roost to breakfast</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 1 of following a covey: at first light or dusk, stand still on a road edge and listen for the chi CA go assembly call. Point toward the sound and note the cover.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 1 Listen</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(70 190)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<path d=\"M90 180 q40 -40 80 0 M100 170 q30 -30 60 0\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"60\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"300\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">&quot;chi CA go&quot;</text>\n<g transform=\"translate(300 160) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-28 -6 L-26 4 Z\" fill=\"#5f6168\"/><ellipse cx=\"-2\" cy=\"6\" rx=\"14\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#c9b48a\"/><path d=\"M-10 4 l3 3 M-4 4 l3 3 M2 4 l3 3 M8 4 l3 3\" stroke=\"#5f6168\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><path d=\"M-12 -4 l14 -2 M-12 0 l14 -2\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/><path d=\"M14 -10 a7 7 0 0 0 9 6 L22 -2 a9 9 0 0 1 -9 -8 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M12 -9 q4 9 12 6\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" fill=\"none\"/><path d=\"M14 -19 q-2 -10 8 -9 q-4 1 -5 9 Z\" fill=\"#111\"/><circle cx=\"19\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#333\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 8 M8 12 l2 8\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dawn or dusk: stand still, listen</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> First light: the covey calls from the roost trees.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 2: walk the road edge toward the calls and read the sign: tracks, droppings and dusting bowls show where the covey feeds and loafs.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Follow a covey: 2 Read the sign</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"40\" width=\"380\" height=\"196\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"170\" width=\"380\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#e6d3b0\"/>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M120 200 L120 178\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L110.1 182.4\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L129.9 182.4\"/><path d=\"M120 200 L120 203.96\"/></g>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M160 196 L160 174\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L150.1 178.4\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L169.9 178.4\"/><path d=\"M160 196 L160 199.96\"/></g>\n<g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M200 200 L200 178\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L190.1 182.4\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L209.9 182.4\"/><path d=\"M200 200 L200 203.96\"/></g>\n<ellipse cx=\"270\" cy=\"190\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"300\" cy=\"110\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"34\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks</text>\n<text x=\"270\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dust bowl</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"246\" width=\"380\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"269\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tracks and dust bowls point to cover</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> They walk out to lane edges for grit and seeds.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where to look for quail, map view. A creek with brushy edges, blackberry and rose thickets beside an orchard and a grain field, and a dirt road with tracks and dusting spots near the brush. Stars mark the best spots: thick brush right beside food.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <rect x=\"250\" y=\"20\" width=\"140\" height=\"120\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f6e3b\">\n    <circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"40\" r=\"6\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"70\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"70\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"70\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"70\" r=\"6\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"360\" cy=\"100\" r=\"6\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"132\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">orchard</text>\n  <rect x=\"250\" y=\"170\" width=\"140\" height=\"110\" fill=\"#e3c97a\"/>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"230\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">grain</text>\n  <path d=\"M120 0 C 140 80, 100 160, 140 300\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"50\"/>\n  <path d=\"M120 0 C 140 80, 100 160, 140 300\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#6b7a50\"><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"18\"/><circle cx=\"222\" cy=\"160\" r=\"16\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"60\" r=\"16\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"210\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">thickets</text>\n  <path d=\"M0 260 L250 250\" stroke=\"#c9b79c\" stroke-width=\"16\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">dirt road: tracks, dust spots</text>\n  <g fill=\"#e8590c\"><polygon points=\"232,124 236,134 246,134 238,140 241,150 232,144 223,150 226,140 218,134 228,134\"/><polygon points=\"232,204 236,214 246,214 238,220 241,230 232,224 223,230 226,220 218,214 228,214\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Brushy creek</text>\n  <text x=\"12\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Stars: brush beside food (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> They feed along brush that sits beside food.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Top view of a dirt lane beside a brush edge. Shallow round dusting bowls in the dirt, small three toed tracks, and a grey body feather. Washington Fish and Wildlife says dusting holes, tracks and droppings show quail are near, 75 percent. Tip: dusting happens at midday, so check the spot then.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting bowls on a dirt lane</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" fill=\"#e6d3b0\"/>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">brush edge</text>\n<ellipse cx=\"90\" cy=\"140\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"150\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"210\" cy=\"130\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<ellipse cx=\"280\" cy=\"165\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#cdb48a\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M240 200 l-4 -8 M244 200 l0 -9 M248 200 l4 -8 M262 214 l-4 -8 M266 214 l0 -9 M270 214 l4 -8\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M330 120 q10 -8 16 2 q-8 4 -16 -2 Z\" fill=\"#7d7f86\"/>\n<text x=\"338\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">feather</text>\n<text x=\"150\" y=\"196\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">bowls</text>\n<text x=\"254\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">tracks</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"236\" width=\"380\" height=\"56\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Dusting holes, tracks, droppings: birds near (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Midday dusting spot: come back at noon (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> By midday they dust and rest near cover.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><ul><li>Be in place, quiet, at first light (Tip).</li><li>Listen before you walk (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: mornings in full</summary><ul><li>Roosts: dense trees or shrubs, not on the ground (70%, Birder's Handbook).</li><li>The morning feed starts just after dawn <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Grit before feeding <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Feeding stays close to cover: seldom more than 15 to 30 m out <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Tip: on a frosty morning, birds may wait for sun on the brush before moving. A late start can pay.</li><li>Note the legal start: 1 hour before sunrise <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. It is often too dark to name a quail then. No shot until you can see the plume (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Body heat card. Bird body temperature is about 41 to 41.7 degrees Celsius, chicken figure, 70 percent. Cold: feathers fluffed and quail roost in dense trees or shrubs, not on the ground, 70 percent. Hot: birds pant, rest in shade midday and in hot weather need free water every day, 80 percent from California wildlife habitat records.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Body heat</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"40\" width=\"80\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<rect x=\"190\" y=\"56\" width=\"20\" height=\"100\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"194\" y=\"80\" width=\"12\" height=\"76\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"168\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">41 to 41.7 °C (70%)</text>\n<rect x=\"12\" y=\"40\" width=\"140\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe8f2\"/>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">COLD</text>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Fluff feathers</text>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Roost in thick</text>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">trees or shrubs</text>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">off the ground</text>\n<text x=\"82\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">(70%)</text>\n<rect x=\"248\" y=\"40\" width=\"140\" height=\"150\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f6e0d2\"/>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">HOT</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pant, sit in</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">shade midday</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Need water</text>\n<text x=\"318\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">every day (80%)</text>\n<rect x=\"10\" y=\"232\" width=\"380\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"256\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hot dry day: hunt near water and shade</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Cold day: sunny edges near roost trees (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Hot, dry day: they need water daily <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Midday they rest in thick cover and are hard to flush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: midday in full</summary><ul><li>In hot weather quail need free water every day; in cool weather green plants, insects and dew can be enough (80%, California habitat records).</li><li>They gather near water in dry weather and spread out when green plants and water are plentiful <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>\"During the middle of the day, especially when it's hot, they tend to hold tight in thicker cover.\" (60%, Field and Stream, search preview)</li><li>Chukar: feed through the morning, then move to shady slopes and draws, dusting sites and water holes at midday (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife). They spend the hottest part of the day in shade (80%, FEIS).</li><li>Tip: a midday break for you too. Clean birds, rest the dog, then hunt the last 2 hours.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Evidence bars for weather claims. Hot dry weather, quail need water daily: 80 percent. Storms, they feed in the breaks: 70 percent. A hawk about, they may skip the afternoon feed: 70 percent. Wind, gray partridge shelter in lee cover: 60 percent. Cold fronts and barometric pressure moving birds: no good data, a Tip only. Moon phase: no good data, a Tip only.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Weather and the day: how sure?</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hot dry day: drink daily</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"44\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"44\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"63\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">80%</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Storm: feed in the breaks</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"82\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"82\" width=\"105.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">70%</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Hawk about: skip a meal</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"120\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"120\" width=\"105.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"139\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">70%</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Windy: hide in lee cover</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"158\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"158\" width=\"90.0\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"start\">60%</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Cold front: moves birds?</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"196\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"215\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"start\">no good data: Tip</text>\n<text x=\"222\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Moon phase: matters?</text>\n<rect x=\"230\" y=\"234\" width=\"150\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#efe9dc\"/>\n<text x=\"236\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#a33b2a\" text-anchor=\"start\">no good data: Tip</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Windy row: Huns, Washington data</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Storms: they feed in the breaks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Cold fronts, pressure and moon: no good data, Tip only.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: weather in full, with evidence</summary><ul><li>Rain and storms: \"During storms they feed sporadically throughout the day during breaks in the storm.\" (70%, Edgewood notes)</li><li>Heat and drought: water every day; birds gather near water <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Wind: Huns take shelter behind tree lines, fence rows, boulders, buildings, in narrow draws and on lee hillsides (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife). For quail, wind makes birds hard to hear and flighty: Tip.</li><li>Snow: chukar gather where snow is thin; south slopes after cold nights <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>. Quail move to sunny slopes and bare ground (Tip, 60%).</li><li>Cold fronts and barometric pressure: many hunters say birds feed hard before a front. No quail study found: Tip, <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>.</li><li>Moon: no quail data found. Quail are day birds and roost at night <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>, so moon effects are unlikely to matter much (Tip).</li><li>Cooper's hawk about: quail may skip the second feeding and stay close to cover (70%, Edgewood notes).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Diagram of rings around a hunter. The first flush is close, the second flush farther, the third farther still. Washington Fish and Wildlife says gray partridge flush farther on each approach, and pressured quail near trees may fly up and perch, 75 percent. Lesson: make the first chance count.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pressure teaches them: each flush is farther</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"40\" width=\"400\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(50 140)\"><circle r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"0\" y=\"-16\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">You</text></g>\n<path d=\"M50 84.0 A70 56.0 0 0 1 50 196.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(120 150) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"120\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1st</text>\n<path d=\"M50 52 A130 88 0 0 1 50 228\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(180 130) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2nd</text>\n<path d=\"M50 52 A200 88 0 0 1 50 228\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#a33b2a\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 6\"/>\n<g transform=\"translate(250 110) scale(0.6 0.6)\"><ellipse cx=\"0\" cy=\"0\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"13\" fill=\"#8f9396\"/><path d=\"M-18 -2 L-27 -4 L-25 5 Z\" fill=\"#b5652b\"/><path d=\"M-6 4 q6 -6 12 0 q-6 4 -12 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b3a1e\"/><circle cx=\"16\" cy=\"-12\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#d9822b\"/><circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"-13\" r=\"1.6\" fill=\"#111\"/><path d=\"M23 -12 l4 1 l-4 2 Z\" fill=\"#555\"/><path d=\"M2 12 l-2 7 M8 12 l2 7\" stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n<text x=\"250\" y=\"162\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3rd</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Huns: farther on the 2nd and 3rd approach (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"274\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Quail near trees may fly up and perch (75%)</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">So: make the first chance count (75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Pressured birds run more and flush wilder (60 to 75%).</li><li>Pushed birds near trees may perch up out of reach <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pressure in full</summary><ul><li>Huns flush farther each time they are pushed (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife).</li><li>Quail flushed near trees may fly up and perch. Washington Fish and Wildlife suggests walking away and coming back 30 to 60 minutes later, when they may be back on the ground <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Do not shoot sitting birds in trees: it is not sporting and a low shot into branches is a safety risk (Tip).</li><li>On busy weekends, hunt a weekday (Tip, from the trip plan).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Hour</th><th>Chukar (75 to 80%)</th><th>Gray partridge <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dawn</td><td>South slopes after cold nights</td><td>Edges of grain fields</td></tr><tr><td>Morning</td><td>Feed, often toward water</td><td>Feed in weedy patches</td></tr><tr><td>Midday</td><td>Shade, dust, water</td><td>Rest in hay, tall grass, fence lines</td></tr><tr><td>Late day</td><td>Climb back to steep roosts</td><td>Feed again (Tip)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Chukar: be above them late in the day (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: chukar and Hun days in full</summary><ul><li>Chukar forage in early morning and late afternoon, usually on the way to water (80%, FEIS). Roost on the ground under sage, juniper or rock outcrops, often in tail to tail coveys <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>\"They'll usually begin moving back toward steeper roosting areas late in the afternoon.\" (75%, Washington Fish and Wildlife)</li><li>Huns feed around grain field edges and weedy patches; they roost, hide and rest in hay fields, tall grass, brush and fence lines <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Hun afternoon pattern: Tip, no source.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A quail day as a timeline chart. Morning: feed at the edges of cover. Midday: rest inside shrubs. Evening: feed again. Night: roost in trees. Best hunting, my opinion: first 2 hours after legal light and last 2 hours before sunset.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A quail day</text>\n  <g font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"14\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <rect x=\"10\" y=\"50\" width=\"90\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"55\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\">Morning</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">feed</text>\n    <rect x=\"105\" y=\"50\" width=\"90\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\">Midday</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">in shrubs</text>\n    <rect x=\"200\" y=\"50\" width=\"90\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\">Evening</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">feed</text>\n    <rect x=\"295\" y=\"50\" width=\"95\" height=\"70\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"342\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#fff\">Night</text><text x=\"342\" y=\"100\" fill=\"#fff\">roost, trees</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Pattern from bird guides (75%)</text>\n  <rect x=\"10\" y=\"168\" width=\"380\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hunt: first 2 hours after legal light,</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">last 2 hours before sunset (Tip)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A lookout bird watches while others feed (75%)</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Calm days, after leaves drop: easier (Tip)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>First 2 hours after legal light you can see in, and the last 2 hours before sunset. Calm, cool days. Midday: rest and clean birds.</p></aside><ul><li>This matches the bird guides' two feeds <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why this lean</summary><ul><li>Two feeds a day, morning and late afternoon (70 to 75%).</li><li>Morning and late afternoon calling helps you find coveys <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>The quick lesson already says: \"Best time, my opinion: the first 2 hours after legal light and the last 2 hours before sunset, on calm days.\" (Tip)</li><li>Give coveys time to regroup before dark: stop a little early (Tip, Tall Timbers manners rule, 60%).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Twenty four hour clock of a quail day in fall, general pattern from bird guides and Washington Fish and Wildlife, 70 to 75 percent. Night: roost in dense trees or shrubs. First light: the covey leaves the roost after assembly calls. Morning: feed and pick grit at road edges. Midday: loaf in cover, dust bathe and drink. Late afternoon: feed again. Dusk: a calling chorus, then roost.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A quail day (October, general pattern)</text>\n<path d=\"M200.0 66.0 A92 92 0 0 1 291.2 170.0 L251.6 164.8 A52 52 0 0 0 200.0 106.0 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M291.2 170.0 A92 92 0 0 1 285.0 193.2 L248.0 177.9 A52 52 0 0 0 251.6 164.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M285.0 193.2 A92 92 0 0 1 235.2 243.0 L219.9 206.0 A52 52 0 0 0 248.0 177.9 Z\" fill=\"#e89b5c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M235.2 243.0 A92 92 0 0 1 134.9 223.1 L163.2 194.8 A52 52 0 0 0 219.9 206.0 Z\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M134.9 223.1 A92 92 0 0 1 108.8 170.0 L148.4 164.8 A52 52 0 0 0 163.2 194.8 Z\" fill=\"#e89b5c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M108.8 170.0 A92 92 0 0 1 108.8 146.0 L148.4 151.2 A52 52 0 0 0 148.4 164.8 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<path d=\"M108.8 146.0 A92 92 0 0 1 200.0 66.0 L200.0 106.0 A52 52 0 0 0 148.4 151.2 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"131.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text>\n<text x=\"232.0\" y=\"163.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"195.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text>\n<text x=\"168.0\" y=\"163.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">18</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">first light:</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"138\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"start\">leave roost</text>\n<text x=\"296\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"start\">feed + grit</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">loaf, dust, water</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"236\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">feed again</text>\n<text x=\"104\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">dusk calls</text>\n<text x=\"110\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">roost in trees</text>\n<text x=\"200\" y=\"294\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A sketch from bird guides (70 to 75%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Rhyme:</strong> \"Call at dawn, grit and feed; dust at noon, then feed at need.\" (Tip)</li><li><strong>Number trick:</strong> \"2 feeds, 2 hours, 2 ends\": feed twice a day <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>; hunt 2 hours at each end of the day (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: more hooks</summary><ul><li><strong>Weather hook:</strong> \"Hot means water, wind means lee, storm means breaks.\" (70 to 80%)</li><li><strong>Old hand's rule (opinion):</strong> \"Walk away from a covey in the trees. Come back in an hour.\" From Washington Fish and Wildlife advice <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li></ul></details>","<ul><li>Edgewood notes, Washington Fish and Wildlife, California habitat records, FEIS, Field and Stream. Checked 2026-10-11.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: every source and date checked</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://friendsofedgewood.org/?p=5231\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Friends of Edgewood: California quail (Franks 2002, from Calkins et al. 1999)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11: feeding twice a day, roost departure, storms, hawks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68963\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Washington Fish and Wildlife: quail hunting</a>, <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68922\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">chukar hunting</a>, <a href=\"https://wdfw.wa.gov/node/68921\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">gray partridge hunting</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://ncrcd.specialdistrict.org/files/b900df31f/California-Quail-info.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">California Wildlife Habitat Relationships: California quail</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fs.usda.gov/database/feis/animals/bird/alch/all.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">US Forest Service FEIS: chukar</a>, read directly 2026-10-11 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.fieldandstream.com/hunting/california-quail-species-profile/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Field and Stream: California quail species profile (Bourjaily 2026)</a>, read directly 2026-10-11; the midday quote is from a companion piece, search preview <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://gardenandgun.com/southern-conundrum-is-it-okay-to-hunt-singles-after-you-flush-a-covey-of-quail\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Garden and Gun with Tall Timbers (2022)</a> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Rules: <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">Rule Book: legal methods, hunting hours</a>, 2 October 2026 edition <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]